feature: G_SP
built by: skill/scripts/apply_signalp.py, not fasta-cluster-pssm-2.pl
departures: not applicable -- this feature has no collection to cluster. The
  signal peptide is a coordinate operation on the curated G alignments: SignalP
  6.0 (fast mode, --organism eukarya) was run on one consensus N-terminus per G
  cluster, and apply_signalp.py cut each cluster's members at the predicted site
  after verifying it against them.
SignalP: 6.0, conda env `signalp`, invoked as `conda run -n signalp signalp6`.
  The env's model_weights/ directory was EMPTY on 18 Nov 2026 and every
  prediction failed; distilled_model_signalp6.pt was restored from the licensed
  tarball already on this machine (Rhabdoviridae/box_folder/Claude/
  signalp-6.0i.fast.tar.gz, downloaded 10 Sep 2026). Nothing was re-downloaded.
predictions: 6 of 7 clusters carry a signal peptide at p = 0.80-0.97, cleaving
  after residue 19-25; the first mature residue is the modal residue in 98-100%
  of each cluster's members.
withheld:
  cluster 7 -- by apply_signalp.py: self-recall 20.5 bits, below the 30-bit
    cutoff a caller needs.
  clusters 4 and 5 -- by hand, see PROVENANCE and withheld/: their profiles
    disagree with GP_N about where the mature protein starts and called signal
    peptides of up to 52 aa.
bit_cutoff: 36, measured. Calls scoring 39.6-56.2 bits put the GP_N start
  exactly one base after the G_SP end on every exemplar; calls at 25.7-31.5
  bits drift by 3-15 nt. The feature calls on 11 of 36 exemplars and tiles the
  precursor exactly on all 11.
note: this is a PREDICTION. No bornavirus signal peptide has been determined
  experimentally. Its only corroboration is that removing it leaves a 230 aa
  mature N-terminal subunit, about 27 kDa deglycosylated, which is what
  Kiermayer 2002 measured for GP-N (PMID 12417322).
